Short answer: I did not find an existing “current user session/me” API endpoint in the searched results that returns admin + group membership for client-side gating. What I did find shows $empMembership is primarily populated server-side and injected into Smarty templates.

What I found
1) How $empMembership is populated server-side
In software/LEAF, multiple PHP entrypoints assign membership directly from login/session objects into Smarty:

LEAF_Request_Portal/report.php assigns:
empUID via $login->getEmpUID()
empMembership via $login->getMembership()
orgchartPath via $site_paths['orgchart_path']
LEAF_Nexus/report.php similarly assigns empMembership via $oc_login->getMembership()
LEAF_Nexus/index.php checks admin using membership group 1:
isset($memberships['groupID'][1]) or $oc_login->getMembership()['groupID'][1]
So the Smarty pattern ($empMembership['groupID'][X]) is coming from getMembership() on the login object, then template injection.

2) Admin check pattern
I found repeated server-side logic:

admin = group 1 membership (groupID[1]), e.g. in LEAF_Nexus/index.php and LEAF_Nexus/report.php.
That strongly suggests admin status is currently computed/checked in PHP during render, not via a dedicated “whoami” JSON endpoint in these hits.

3) Existing API wrappers / client convention
I found app/libs/js/portal/LEAFPortalAPI.js and libs/jsapi/nexus/LEAFNexusAPI.js using $.ajax for API calls (GET/POST).
So existing convention is jQuery AJAX, not fetch in these references.

4) orgchartPath usage
orgchartPath is passed from PHP into Smarty (report.php etc.) as a path variable for client/template use.
In the returned hits, I did not see a clear endpoint definition showing a direct “permissions/status” JSON response tied to orgchartPath; it appears to be a base path handoff rather than itself a user-permissions endpoint.

Endpoints found relevant to your question
From searched hits, I did not find a definitive endpoint like:

/api/me
/api/session
/api/currentUser
endpoint returning { isAdmin, empUID, memberships }
I did find many functional APIs (form/group/indicator etc.), but none in these results clearly expose current logged-in user membership/admin as a standalone JSON route.

Auth / CSRF pattern observed
Session-based auth is in use (PHP session setup; PHPSESSID cookie).
CSRF token is assigned to templates ($_SESSION['CSRFToken']) and used on POSTs in JS wrappers.
GETs are typically plain AJAX GETs with session cookie; POSTs include CSRF token in payload.
